  "corrections": [
    "Move to indicator lesson after linearity and indicators are taught; random-variable lesson keeps its die-mean question.",
    "Rounded logarithmic exponent is approximate, not exactly equal.",
    "Rounded exponentials must use approximate equality.",
    "Rounded logarithm is approximate, not exact.",
    "New distinct colliding keys compare against zero through n minus one existing keys, not one through n.",
    "Clarify exact comparison-count model.",
    "A p-value is a tail probability of the specified statistic, not universally the unstandardised difference.",
    "Keep interpretation consistent with statistic definition.",
    "Rare true effects alone does not determine false-discovery probability.",
    "A six-sigma outcome is possible under the null; it supports investigation without proving a defect.",
    "Make measurability consistent with general event definition.",
    "Restore natural title after glossary-oriented circumlocution.",
    "Use established technical name; reviewed Discrete definition will support alias.",
    "Use sufficient harmonic-number precision for reported rounded result.",
    "Remove duplicated label.",
    "Every probability/conditional/expectation/variance card now states its measurable-event, positive conditioning, finite-expectation and finite-second-moment domains locally. Underlying identities independently reviewed; no equation or executable code changed in this pass.",
    "Separate the collection of events from a single measurable event; event-space alias formerly opened the latter.",
    "Additive smoothing is broader than add-one; preserve alias with correct general definition.",
    "State convergence without suggesting monotonic improvement.",
    "Not all quantile sketches support arbitrary merging.",
    "Fan-out does not inherently require waiting for all responses.",
    "t-distribution alias must describe the distribution as well as the interval; require positive degrees of freedom.",
    "Storage engines are not restricted to disk.",
    "Bits-per-key aliases must define the memory ratio rather than only the error probability.",
    "Distinguish iid multinomial token likelihoods used by code/add-one smoothing from document-presence Bernoulli likelihoods supplied by questions; these probabilities are not interchangeable.",
    "Tighten local formula definitions for finite counts, uniform permutation/token/hash/quicksort models, estimated standard error, and positive integer Bloom hash choices.",
    "Reviewed actual foreign dictionary meanings: detection-rate wording avoids cache hit-rate popup; expectation-of-square avoids signal-power popup; equality tests avoid sorting-order popup; request/service wording avoids endpoint/thread-pool type assumptions; interval approximation avoids sampling-period popup; natural exponential avoids an inaccurate foreign pitch/frequency example; explicit sorted rank avoids ambiguous index convention.",
    "Source-support review replaces unrelated/broad reference pages: classification accuracy is distinct from measurement accuracy; pooled proportion differs from pooled variance; common-mode failures differ from Shewhart common causes; NIST sampling section replaces frameset; original Tail at Scale PDF replaces navigation-heavy landing page. All new primary pages fetched/read independently.",
    "Clarify probability-weighted absolute expectation sum. Remove unnecessary independent-metric prompt carveout now that the true option explicitly covers general dependence; retain independence only in the illustrative 64% calculation. Existing conceptual answers and answer indices remain unchanged.",
    "Full own-subject context audit: product-sign Π and variable p_0 avoid mathematical-pi popovers; mean-duration avoids worst-input algorithm-runtime popover; shrinking geometric tails avoid exponential-growth popover. Use explicit pivot-choice maxima and expected-cost analysis instead of input-distribution worst/average-case popovers. Avoid Complexity06’s direction-specific any-accept amplification definition pending owner correction; no donor source edited.",
    "Reviewed all301 complete glossary popup fields, including linked definitions. Corrected sample-space omega vs complexity Omega, probabilistic product identity vs combinatorial product rule, infrastructure failure domains vs logical domains, flaky outcomes vs automaton nondeterminism, coordinate plots vs discrete graphs, intervals vs rate-limit fixed windows, distribution vs exponential growth, Gaussian values vs normal floats, queue fullness vs integer overflow, packet loss vs lossy compression, statistical hypotheses vs Hypothesis library, unique Git prefixes vs regex ambiguity, and DOS vs HTTP503. Added precise statistical-hypothesis-test entry; ham now cites primary SpamAssassin documentation.",
    "Final numeric-notation review excludes zero from the zero-power identity and correctly labels1.96 as a rounded normal quantile rather than an exact value."
  ],
